    {"course":"MTH 201","module":"Partial fractions and reduction formulas","lesson":"Partial fractions with distinct linear factors","key":"fos-practice-fraction-distinct-1","prompt":"Write 1/[(x−1)(x−3)] = A/(x−1) + B/(x−3). Find B.","options":null,"aliases":["0.5","1/2"],"explanation":"Clear the denominators and evaluate at x equal to the second root. This leaves 1=2B."},
