    {"course":"MTH 201","module":"Partial fractions and reduction formulas","lesson":"Reduction formulas for exponential integrals","key":"fos-practice-fraction-exp-1","prompt":"When integrating x^1e^(2x) by parts with u=x^1, what coefficient multiplies the remaining integral, including its sign?","options":null,"aliases":["-0.5","-1/2"],"explanation":"Use v=e^(2x)/2 and subtract ∫v du. The coefficient is −i/2."},
