    {"course":"MTH 201","module":"Curve analysis and stationary points","lesson":"Inflection points require a change of concavity","key":"fos-practice-curve-noinflect-1","prompt":"At x=1, the second derivative of (x−1)⁴ is zero. What is the correct classification for its concavity there?","options":null,"aliases":["No inflection point","no inflection","not an inflection point"],"explanation":"The second derivative is 12(x−i)², nonnegative on both sides."},
