    {"course":"PHY 101","module":"Fluid mechanics and dimensions","lesson":"Dimensions and viscous flow","key":"fos-practice-fluid-dimensions-1","prompt":"A relation is proposed as F = k m^(1) a, where F is force and a is acceleration. What exponent of mass must k carry?","options":null,"aliases":["0"],"explanation":"Force has one power of mass. After accounting for m raised to the given power, k carries the remainder."},
