    {"course":"PHY 107","module":"Buoyancy and apparent weight","lesson":"Upthrust and apparent weight","key":"fos-practice-buoyancy-difference-1","prompt":"A solid weighs 9 N in air and 4 N when fully submerged in water. Find the upthrust in N.","options":null,"aliases":["5"],"explanation":"Upthrust is the loss of apparent weight: the air reading minus the submerged reading."},
